From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:30:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: prores: import the ProRes encoder from
 aurora

Import the Apple ProRes encoder driver (APR) from aurora-silicon/linux
integration/aurora 2362d9a55b, file for file: every file under
drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/ is identical to that tree. Hook it
into the Apple media Kconfig and Makefile next to the scaler, and build
it as a module in asahi.config, as aurora does.

The driver is a V4L2 memory-to-memory encoder for the T6000 and T8140
engines (ProRes 422 Proxy to 4444 XQ). It binds only those two
compatibles, so it binds nothing on a T8132 machine.

Upstream history of these files (all by Ryan Murray): the driver
1ee8f88e57, per-profile rate control 81ff08af9f, T8140 performance
requests a02f819f05, the T6000 APR a0 descriptor 186ce02e0e, compatible
matching db20caf533 and T6000 rate budgets 0c521040cf.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 7d906c5d38fd02c3c23db33612b7214ec6cfae7a)
